& ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}+(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+144{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{16({cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta ))}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )+9{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15131/selection/e99dc8121eda3ffdd610f54ac8244f9bca6a6058031b4dea3921f040d5f3eb00" :answer/id #uuid "8c5d3b58-7e8a-5f6d-86a2-5ed24d688554" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15131/selection/4866f1e761740a4730b716e68ff43bfef7813733ef845d19f5b15f55ce6b8b0b" :answer/id #uuid "523aed49-b3ee-5395-b90d-eb46c6131ffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15131/selection/45e63f5edfe1db585dcf18ece801c44f4620f4d629b8dbfc9fdaef62806d4067" :answer/id #uuid "bc56044d-8fda-5276-8394-af9fcdc502dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15131/selection/ebbf233321aae27ee6748ece170c9587a86197b6399ec8ef708ecaec3145b352" :answer/id #uuid "2e72ec29-1d01-5804-ac42-d1b7e752ced7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15131/selection/b762b453b65f1016138cb40fbeafbadc4adcc3301dd41c49a37b25d7724476fd" :answer/id #uuid "6b958f01-aa6c-5b61-9d6d-c1f451e90c88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15131/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "82449739-797f-5c53-85f1-ec698694ff5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15131/selection/45e63f5edfe1db585dcf18ece801c44f4620f4d629b8dbfc9fdaef62806d4067" :answer-field/choices ["q-15131/selection/e99dc8121eda3ffdd610f54ac8244f9bca6a6058031b4dea3921f040d5f3eb00" "q-15131/selection/4866f1e761740a4730b716e68ff43bfef7813733ef845d19f5b15f55ce6b8b0b" "q-15131/selection/45e63f5edfe1db585dcf18ece801c44f4620f4d629b8dbfc9fdaef62806d4067" "q-15131/selection/ebbf233321aae27ee6748ece170c9587a86197b6399ec8ef708ecaec3145b352" "q-15131/selection/b762b453b65f1016138cb40fbeafbadc4adcc3301dd41c49a37b25d7724476fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15131" :question/id #uuid "39db532b-b9fa-5609-9541-05b798626edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-15131" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/00e5e0f5c47a056beaca2d7bc1b1d10a6a11f96398df7400e69c023f5780b8a6.png)\n\nWhich of the following integrals gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $-\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the  diagram above)?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+1+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )+3{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15131/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0b4da9-1a0f-5a46-aff1-3ce5c0cebb3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15131"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20070/selection/f4e28b619e7a6193840f290c4ee4b1ecbe82c44107b1b0e9ea324aba0c54293d" :answer/id #uuid "7de1217e-7df7-5c94-8bd2-95e6bd28e197" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{\\pi /4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20070/selection/66398b555907fb576465a142f37f227fd8de20fc53a16f896f467ab4798db339" :answer/id #uuid "aaf02204-23e8-5e54-a4dd-0835514589fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /4}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20070/selection/f6eef8201715cd35152f2e04a176270ab86d24ea3457b098d3d30565efc61ccd" :answer/id #uuid "64de7071-e0e2-52b9-a70e-48a7c56e596b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20070/selection/8b9ca36335d00e31217f0aa26cfe3da395bed36d45dc188e8aed44375e6922a6" :answer/id #uuid "f2cc63ef-146d-5d35-9c03-aa861095956e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20070/selection/3e82b99cc9914fdfeef375126c50581f0477e6f04550d0694a54af4ddf19c2eb" :answer/id #uuid "a4db64b8-39e3-5c3b-bc74-edf065084c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{-\\pi /4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20070/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b447a4-4384-55a0-831a-bdb7fbf86d1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20070/selection/8b9ca36335d00e31217f0aa26cfe3da395bed36d45dc188e8aed44375e6922a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-20070/selection/f4e28b619e7a6193840f290c4ee4b1ecbe82c44107b1b0e9ea324aba0c54293d" "q-20070/selection/66398b555907fb576465a142f37f227fd8de20fc53a16f896f467ab4798db339" "q-20070/selection/f6eef8201715cd35152f2e04a176270ab86d24ea3457b098d3d30565efc61ccd" "q-20070/selection/8b9ca36335d00e31217f0aa26cfe3da395bed36d45dc188e8aed44375e6922a6" "q-20070/selection/3e82b99cc9914fdfeef375126c50581f0477e6f04550d0694a54af4ddf19c2eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20070" :question/id #uuid "eeba4fa8-124a-54c9-ba6c-4f189488c740" :question/math-academy-id "q-20070" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/fa1c1c3ae2769f45854de4f0b00fc394fccb40b40704cfd09e6eb11eee3c07af.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=3{e}^{\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(3{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{e}^{2\\theta }+9{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{18{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-20070/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103837/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "d39a51d1-6c5c-57a5-9796-d211cb101219" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103837/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9908c519-14e1-52f3-8311-104bd61b6519" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103837/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d0b9f012-351f-59bb-8d52-8b4275f79e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103837/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "6f7aaa83-03b2-50b0-85ad-04f7fedce162" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103837/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "7c5bae57-7c8b-5823-82d9-ed49119b22a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103837/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9da43ea2-e27e-53f4-b67c-512326b3df0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103837/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-103837/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-103837/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-103837/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-103837/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-103837/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103837" :question/id #uuid "a9fbe6a6-9f8e-565c-aaf7-05ef27741553" :question/math-academy-id "q-103837" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/3387790df770ac8645058c6f460b1f1285629d18d765668e362a8070ae4035ed.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ (shown in blue in the diagram above).\n\n*Hint: You may wish to use the following identity: $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall the identity for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using $x=\\theta $ in the previous identity, the integral can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={4\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103837/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103837"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353598/field-1/141552b538f4607f1d24c18cbba875462b38d3232088d132a780f85bc39dc9cd" :answer/id #uuid "5d05a954-59b2-5a95-8e0d-489514000361" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(e^{\\pi}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353598/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6facb5aa-f66d-5704-b851-c125a1e4ce3a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353598/field-1/141552b538f4607f1d24c18cbba875462b38d3232088d132a780f85bc39dc9cd" :answer-field/choices ["q-353598/field-1/141552b538f4607f1d24c18cbba875462b38d3232088d132a780f85bc39dc9cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353598" :question/id #uuid "11886f6e-15f4-57af-a1dd-d57334eb5acd" :question/math-academy-id "q-353598" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/16b676776dc22aece5a1fa777007a03b9e7903706cbdf5cc4ae14d8508370419.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the polar curve $r={e}^{2\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={e}^{2\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2{e}^{2\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({e}^{2\\theta })}^{2}+{(2{e}^{2\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{4\\theta }+4{e}^{4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{5{e}^{4\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\theta }]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{[{e}^{2\\theta }]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{2(\\pi /2)}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}({e}^{\\pi }-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353598/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353598"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-9532"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/085be1e624ae99afee256d2a9591f17d2f33f688364b6e59fdcd7c415206bda7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta {|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-103842/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "daa42cd4-4db7-5533-8487-a93fc0cac64f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103842/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "8278f486-59bc-511b-a61d-a5238f955185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103842/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "7c08066b-0479-533d-a16b-b52cd247bfa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103842/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer/id #uuid "d38eb521-7a96-5178-b92f-e2a75a3db002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103842/selection/03823734f5a6acf01bf34858799ade5010e90ee3423ea03ba13a6528b66df155" :answer/id #uuid "8fdfb116-59fb-5643-9cb2-f472155ca79d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103842/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6683086e-5d52-51db-bf84-62688cf65d6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103842/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer-field/choices ["q-103842/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-103842/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-103842/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-103842/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" "q-103842/selection/03823734f5a6acf01bf34858799ade5010e90ee3423ea03ba13a6528b66df155"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103842" :question/id #uuid "839287cb-e3c9-5af7-9d3b-6508ad20a911" :question/math-academy-id "q-103842" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/038d135bd0d8d163808fe21be0159a1a08db37c3e33599c97033ca0d53abab36.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta {|}_{3\\pi /2}^{7\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103842/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a533e8-9a7c-58f3-9d3c-7c08b3c6bfd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103842"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7400"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/e5647c0f19727d1e626e637464cc57444e0bc0f2f8e99a4afd15d3c3631dc3f0.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the arc length of the polar curve $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi,$ shown in blue in the diagram above." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=3-\\sin(7\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} =-7\\cos(7\\theta)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}+(-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+49{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+1+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\theta )+48{cos}^{2}⁡(7\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-641"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067289/assets/0bb9e5e7315d4bcd5fc21700fdd2597f6d9b585a109145de53c6f94e9530eabf.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta)$ for $0 \\leq \\theta \\leq \\pi$ (shown in blue in the picture above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL =  \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} \\sqrt{r^2 +\\left(\\frac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta}\\right)^2 }\\,\\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nSince $r=2(1-\\cos\\theta),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}\\theta} = 2\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now use the half-angle formula $1-\\cos\\theta =2\\sin^2\\left(\\dfrac{\\theta}{2}\\right)$ to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={-4\\cdot 2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
